fuxi: 0121 -- catch the panic at its entry, with the caller

The ring header proves panics happen here (flush seq 0xffffffff) while the ring content
keeps ending mid-userspace with no cause in it: the tee in debugger_collect_diagnostics
only fires on branches this board does not reliably take, and the note attempts failed
because the buffers they guessed at hold nothing useful at that point.

panic() itself is the one place every panic passes through, with the format string and
the arguments in hand.  It now formats the message there (va_copy, so the real panic
path is unaffected), records "*** FUXI PANIC: caller 0x...: <message>" in the ring, and
guards against a nested panic re-entering the formatter.

The caller address resolves against the kernel binary this build produces, so the
surviving record names both the failure and the function that raised it.

Harness: applied=120 skipped=0.
--- a/osfmk/kern/debug.c
+++ b/osfmk/kern/debug.c
@@ -973,6 +973,33 @@
 	va_list panic_str_args;
 
 	va_start(panic_str_args, str);
+	/*
+	 * Record the panic before anything else can go wrong.
+	 *
+	 * The tee in debugger_collect_diagnostics only fires on branches this board does
+	 * not reliably take, and the ring header proves panics happen (flush seq
+	 * 0xffffffff) while the ring itself keeps ending mid-userspace with no cause in
+	 * it.  Formatting here -- at the entry every panic goes through -- with the
+	 * caller address, makes the surviving record name both the failure and who
+	 * raised it, and 0x... resolves against the kernel binary this build produces.
+	 */
+	{
+		extern void fuxi_log_panic_note(const char *text);
+		static bool fuxi_panic_note_busy;
+		va_list fuxi_copy;
+		char fuxi_msg[224];
+		char fuxi_full[300];
+
+		if (!fuxi_panic_note_busy) {
+			fuxi_panic_note_busy = true;
+			va_copy(fuxi_copy, panic_str_args);
+			vsnprintf(fuxi_msg, sizeof(fuxi_msg), str, fuxi_copy);
+			va_end(fuxi_copy);
+			snprintf(fuxi_full, sizeof(fuxi_full), "caller %p: %s",
+			    __builtin_return_address(0), fuxi_msg);
+			fuxi_log_panic_note(fuxi_full);
+		}
+	}
 	panic_trap_to_debugger(str, &panic_str_args, 0, NULL, 0, NULL, (unsigned long)(char *)__builtin_return_address(0));
 	va_end(panic_str_args);
 }
